# Correct pronunciation

Correct means the way the word is supposed to be said. A recording that matches a rule this project wrote is not correct when that rule was filled in because the pronunciation is unknown.

Say that the pronunciation is unknown. Do not call it correct, confident, or a reading of Dee because the code followed the letter table, the lexicon string, or a test.

```text
# Bad
The recording is correct: ds is the letter-names, and the code spoke them.

# Good
The pronunciation of ds is unknown. The recording is spelling English letter-names because the table has no vowel to speak.
```

A check that the stored string matches the code is a check of the code. Report it as that. It is not evidence the word is pronounced that way.
